# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — ai-repo-template default
# =============================================================================
# This is the template's *default* .gitignore. Derived repos should EXTEND
# this file with project-specific patterns rather than replacing it.
#
# Why this file exists:
#   postmortem-001 (docs/postmortems/postmortem-001-workflow-bypass.md)
#   documented a contributing factor: the downstream repo shipped without a
#   .gitignore, so `terraform init` left ~90 MB of provider binaries in the
#   working tree. If the agent had committed everything, those binaries
#   would have entered git history.
#
# Sibling decisions:
#   - ADR-012 (docs/decisions/adr-012-explicit-workflow-preconditions.md)
#     adds the AGENTS.md branch-precondition rule.
#   - ADR-013 (docs/decisions/adr-013-pre-commit-on-main-default.md)
#     records why we ship .pre-commit-config.yaml.template only and do NOT
#     install a block-commits-to-main hook by default.
#
# What's intentionally NOT here:
#   - .terraform.lock.hcl — convention is to commit dependency lock files.
#   - .env.example — explicitly negated (see `!.env.example` below) so the
#     example file remains tracked even when its `.env*` siblings are not.
# =============================================================================

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.log

# --- Editor / IDE configs (per-developer; commit project-wide settings
#     deliberately under .vscode/settings.json if needed, then add an
#     explicit `!` exception in a derived repo) ---
#     Wildcard form (`.vscode/*`, not `.idea/`) is intentional: Git does
#     not recurse into a directory ignored by `dir/`, so `!.vscode/settings.json`
#     in a derived repo would not work against `.vscode/`. Using `.vscode/*`
#     ignores the contents while keeping the directory itself searchable
#     for `!file` re-includes.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/*

# --- Build / dist outputs ---
dist/
build/
coverage/

# --- Node ---
node_modules/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Terraform (state files only — lock files are committed) ---
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
